 "verdict": {
  "residue": "REMOVED",
  "attributed_to": "#1041 (`a517ea94`), which parameterised the `MapCore` and `ExpanseSet` root-leaf operations over `const OCC` and routed the classic Judy C ABI symbols to the `_plain` entry points",
  "evidence": [
   "bracketing (executed, CI): the arm's Callgrind Ir is bit-identical across the three push runs before `a517ea94` and the two after, and `80884c13..a517ea94` holds exactly one commit",
   "per-function (executed, local aarch64 Callgrind): the -40,487 Ir delta reproduces bit-identically, and 33.2 % of it is the `OnceLock` read machinery and the allocator's atomic RMW helper leaving `JudyLIns` \u2014 `core::sync::atomic` -8,485, `core::cell` -2,291, the LSE `ldadd` helper -2,655",
   "static: `JudyLIns`'s acquire loads go 12 (`fb69a4af`) -> 19 (`728e316e`, section 11.10.10) -> 9 (`636fcaa7`, section 11.10.10; reproduced here at `80884c13`) -> 0 (`a517ea94`), the same ordering as the Ir",
   "the mechanism removed is the one section 11.10.10 predicted: the root-leaf code in `map.rs` was not generic over the mode"
  ],
  "not_established": [
   "66.8 % of the delta (-27,056 Ir) is net redistribution across the monomorphized bodies and is NOT attributed to a single mechanism: map.rs, compat.rs, leaf.rs and bits.rs fall while alloc.rs, `core::ptr` and `core::ptr::non_null` rise. Reported as unexplained (AGENTS.md section 8.20.4)",
   "the static per-site counts are instructions PRESENT; they are not executed counts, and the Ir per static site is not constant across the four commits (7.0, 2.0 and 4.5 Ir/op per site for the three steps), so no per-site cost is claimed",
   "the `strmap_*` arms carry #1001's rewrite of the `SyncExpanseStrMap` write path in the same span, so their net against `fb69a4af` is not attributable to #997 / #1010 / #1041 alone",
   "the aarch64 `map_insert/sequential` arm's -10.867 % against `fb69a4af` is recorded, not attributed; no profile of it was taken"
  ],
  "instrument_that_would_split_the_remainder": "a per-line `callgrind_annotate --auto=yes` of the same two out files, or an inverse ablation restoring the generic root-leaf path at `a517ea94`",
  "what_998_has_left": "on x86, not aarch64: #1041 put four smoke arms over the 0.1 % review threshold against `fb69a4af` \u2014 `judy1_set/sequential` +1.999 %, `judy1_set/random` +0.815 %, `set_insert/sequential` +0.332 %, `judy1_set/clustered` +0.197 % \u2014 where `80884c13` had one (`judysl_insert/routes` +0.558 %, now -0.700 %). The same arms fall on aarch64. #1041's `allow-regression:` line names `set_insert/sequential` on the deterministic job and localises that residue to `leaf::locate` with the mechanism unattributed; it does not name these smoke arms. No x86 profile of them was taken here and none is attributed."
